{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "ARF support implemented in both Go and TypeScript converters, with format detection, CLI alias, and comprehensive tests. All 37 Go converter tests pass (28 XCCDF + 9 ARF), all 61 TypeScript tests pass (48 XCCDF + 13 ARF), all format detection tests pass, and CLI tests pass.", "closed_at": "2026-02-23 03:48:42", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "8003242e1bcb32c85c3b0ae405e3746d2579c02dc1723420711d94ffe0c551ba", "created_at": "2026-02-23 02:46:59", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "ARF (NIST IR 7694) is an XML wrapper format that packages one or more XCCDF TestResults along with asset metadata (IP, hostname, FQDN) and relationships. OpenSCAP and other SCAP scanners produce ARF as their primary output format.\n\nThe XCCDF converter should be extended to:\n1. Detect whether input is raw XCCDF or ARF-wrapped XCCDF (root element is arf:asset-report-collection vs xccdf:Benchmark/TestResult)\n2. If ARF: extract all arf:report elements containing xccdf:TestResult, extract asset metadata from arf:assets, and delegate each TestResult to existing XCCDF conversion logic\n3. Produce a multi-baseline HDF output when multiple TestResults exist (one baseline per report)\n4. Enrich HDF targets with ARF asset identification (IP addresses, MAC addresses, FQDN, hostname)\n5. Register 'arf' as a CLI alias for the xccdf converter (similar to inspec-to-hdf aliasing legacyhdf)\n\nKey ARF structure:\n- Root: arf:asset-report-collection\n- arf:report-requests \u2014 embeds or references the benchmark used\n- arf:assets \u2014 computing-device with IP/MAC/FQDN/hostname\n- arf:reports \u2014 contains one or more arf:report, each wrapping an xccdf:TestResult\n- core:relationships \u2014 links reports to assets via arfvocab:isAbout\n\nSchema: https://csrc.nist.gov/schema/asset-reporting-format/1.1/asset-reporting-format_1.1.0.xsd\nSpec: https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/IR/nistir7694.pdf\n\nThe new findXmlValues utility from hdf-utilities is well-suited for traversing ARF's nested structure to locate TestResult elements and asset metadata.", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-d7m", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "feature", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Add ARF (Asset Reporting Format) support to XCCDF converter", "updated_at": "2026-02-23 03:48:42", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
