{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "", "closed_at": "2026-02-18 23:28:15", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "bd3989c9f89835355ab1d00a98994e227344594f3888d1685e928977f180b61b", "created_at": "2026-02-18 22:30:00", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "Stryker mutation testing scored hdf-parsers at **50.00%** (36 survived, 38 no-coverage) when run on unit tests only. Integration tests were excluded because Stryker's sandbox doesn't include sibling-package fixture files. Stryker config is at `hdf-parsers/stryker.config.cjs`.\n\n## Root cause of low score\nMost survivors and all no-coverage mutations are in code paths only exercised by `integration.test.ts`, which reads fixture files from `hdf-converters/converters/hdf-to-xml/fixtures/`. Stryker cannot reach these files from its `.stryker-tmp` sandbox.\n\n## Cluster 1: Trailing-garbage detection (36 survived / uncovered)\n`parseResults`, `parseBaseline`, and `autoDetect` all have:\n```ts\nconst trimmedInput = jsonStr.trim();\n// ... parse ...\nif (serialized.length !== trimmedInput.length && !isWhitespaceEquivalent(serialized, trimmedInput)) {\n  return { success: false, error: 'Input contains trailing data...' }\n}\n```\nEvery operator and boolean in this condition survived because unit tests don't include inputs with trailing garbage.\n\n## Cluster 2: Schema validation failure path (3 survived)\n`if (!validationResult.valid)` and the error message body survive \u2014 unit tests don't pass structurally invalid JSON (valid JSON, wrong HDF structure).\n\n## Cluster 3: `autoDetect` type narrowing (4 survived)\n`typeof data === 'object' && data !== null` and `'name' in obj && 'requirements' in obj` survive \u2014 unit tests don't call `autoDetect` with an object that lacks these keys.\n\n## Cluster 4: `isWhitespaceEquivalent` (38 no-coverage)\nEntire helper function never called by unit tests.\n\n## Fix options\n1. **Preferred**: Add unit tests that exercise the above paths directly \u2014 pass trailing-garbage JSON, invalid-schema JSON, and objects missing `name`/`requirements`. This avoids the sandbox issue entirely.\n2. **Alternative**: Configure Stryker to include `hdf-converters` fixture files in its sandbox via `symlinkNodeModules: false` and a custom file pattern \u2014 complex, may break other things.\n\n## Priority\nMedium \u2014 the integration tests do cover these paths, so production correctness is verified. This is a test infrastructure gap, not a correctness gap.", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-07n", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 3, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "hdf-parsers: improve mutation test coverage (36 survived, 38 no-cov)", "updated_at": "2026-02-22 19:22:45", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
