{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "", "closed_at": "2026-02-18 23:28:15", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "56c70930fa04646aac345526956ebc35fd62077488bad08e9ffa6c316c4464e7", "created_at": "2026-02-18 22:30:00", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "Stryker mutation testing scored hdf-mappings at **72.48%** (67 survived, 187 killed). Stryker config is at `hdf-mappings/stryker.config.cjs`.\n\n## Survived mutation clusters (affect all or most mapping files)\n\n### 1. Lazy-initialization null checks (8 files \u00d7 2 mutations = ~16 survived)\nEvery mapping module has `if (mappings === null) { mappings = JSON.parse(readFileSync(...)) }`. Mutating to `if (true)` survives because tests always hit a warm cache \u2014 the cold-init path is never independently tested.\n\n**Fix**: Add a test helper that resets the module-level cache variable to `null` between test runs, then assert the function still returns correct data after the reset.\n\n### 2. `'utf-8'` encoding argument (8 files \u00d7 1 mutation = ~8 survived)\n`readFileSync(path, 'utf-8')` \u2014 changing encoding to `\"\"` survives because the test doesn't verify encoding was honored. With `\"\"`, Node returns a Buffer; JSON.parse on a Buffer still works in most cases.\n\n**Fix**: This is somewhat inherent to how Node handles encoding \u2014 consider accepting this survivor as a known false positive, or test with a file containing non-ASCII characters to distinguish Buffer vs string parsing.\n\n### 3. Type guards `||` \u2192 `&&` (cci, nist, owasp \u2014 ~12 mutations)\nPattern: `if (!id || typeof id !== 'string')` \u2014 mutating `||` to `&&` survives because tests don't pass falsy non-string inputs (e.g., `null`, `0`, `false`). The `!id` check already handles those, so the `&&` mutation still rejects them.\n\n**Fix**: Add tests that pass `null`, `undefined`, `0`, `false`, and `123` (number) to each lookup function and assert they return the correct empty/null/false result.\n\n### 4. nikto `typeof id === 'number'` ternary (4 survived)\n`src/nikto/index.ts:30` \u2014 the `typeof niktoId === 'number' ? String(niktoId) : niktoId` coercion is not tested with a numeric argument. Tests only pass strings.\n\n**Fix**: Add a test that passes a numeric Nikto ID and verifies it's correctly coerced to a string for lookup.\n\n### 5. nessus exact/wildcard match logic (several survived)\n`src/nessus/index.ts` \u2014 the exact-match find predicate and wildcard fallback are weakly covered. The wildcard path (`pluginID === '*'`) is not covered at all (4 no-coverage mutations).\n\n**Fix**: Add test cases for: (a) an exact plugin family + ID match, (b) a wildcard match (pluginID === '*'), (c) no match (returns undefined).\n\n### 6. nist regex anchor (1 survived)\n`src/nist/index.ts:105` \u2014 `/^([A-Z]{2})-/` anchor removal survives \u2014 the `^` start anchor isn't tested with a string that has a prefix before the NIST family code.\n\n**Fix**: Test `getNISTFamily('prefix-AC-2')` and verify it returns the correct result (or no match if the regex requires start-of-string).", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-17i", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 3, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "hdf-mappings (TS): improve mutation test coverage (67 survived)", "updated_at": "2026-02-22 19:22:46", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "Implemented: --ca-cert and --insecure flags on all fetchers with shared TLS infrastructure, env var fallback, 11 tests", "closed_at": "2026-03-04 14:59:44", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "ef0488a92d9a71619c5d465e2908406993baa7f2a8a757906773f5b27d70fb06", "created_at": "2026-03-01 01:39:01", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "## Problem\nNone of our API-based fetchers (Splunk, SonarQube, GitLab, AWS Config) support custom CA certificates or insecure TLS bypass. SAF CLI didn't have this either. Users with internal instances behind self-signed or corporate CA certs cannot use live fetch mode.\n\n## Requirements (12-factor CLI best practices)\n1. **--ca-cert <path>** flag: Load a PEM CA bundle for custom certificate authorities (corporate PKI, mkcert, internal CAs)\n2. **--insecure** flag: Skip TLS verification entirely (dev/test only, with a visible warning printed to stderr)\n3. **Environment variable fallback**: Support HDF_CA_CERT and HDF_INSECURE env vars (12-factor: store config in the environment)\n4. Implement once in shared fetcher infrastructure, not per-fetcher\n5. AWS Config fetcher: wire through aws-sdk-go-v2 custom HTTP client\n\n## Design Notes\n- Go: Build a shared `NewHTTPClient(caCertPath string, insecure bool)` in `hdf-cli/internal/fetchers/shared.go` that returns a configured \\*http.Client\n- All fetchers call this instead of `&http.Client{}`\n- --insecure should print a warning to stderr: 'WARNING: TLS certificate verification is disabled. This is insecure.'\n- Cobra flags registered at the parent 'convert' command level so they apply to all fetchers\n- TypeScript: Not needed immediately (CLI is Go-only), but if we add a TS fetcher layer later, use a custom https.Agent with `rejectUnauthorized: false` or `ca: [pemBuffer]`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `hdf convert splunk to hdf --live --ca-cert /path/to/ca.pem ...` works with custom CA\n- [ ] `hdf convert gitlab to hdf --live --insecure ...` works with self-signed certs (prints warning)\n- [ ] HDF_CA_CERT=/path/to/ca.pem hdf convert sonarqube to hdf --live ... works\n- [ ] All fetcher tests still pass (no regression)\n- [ ] --insecure prints visible warning to stderr", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-1bs", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "feature", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "[2026-03-03] Security review finding MED-4 confirms this need. Also fold in MED-2 (default to HTTPS-only, require --allow-insecure-http for plain HTTP fetcher connections to prevent token exposure).", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Add --ca-cert and --insecure TLS flags to all API-based fetchers", "updated_at": "2026-03-04 14:59:44", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
