{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "Resolved via alias: InSpec exec-json is identical to HDF v1.0, so legacyhdf-to-hdf handles it. Added CLI alias (hdf convert inspec to hdf) in b1a1d8d and ubi9 STIG fixture in 686c001.", "closed_at": "2026-02-22 21:20:45", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "3fb858e69f818ab44a3e34b2e2e08592700f1213cf5bf5a2a0d5051c3b919e89", "created_at": "2026-02-20 16:57:36", "created_by": "Will", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "InSpec JSON output needs a dedicated converter for HDF v2. In v1, HDF was structurally derived from InSpec output format, so no converter was needed. In v2, a converter is required.\n\nInSpec JSON output format: { platform: {...}, profiles: [ { name, version, title, controls: [ { id, title, desc, impact, refs, tags, results: [...] } ] } ] }\n\nThis format is the same as the legacyhdf-to-hdf converter input. The inspec-to-hdf converter should:\n- Be a thin, well-named wrapper that clearly targets current InSpec output (v4/v5+)\n- Set dataSource.name = 'Chef InSpec' and dataSource.version from the InSpec version field in output\n- Handle multi-profile InSpec runs (one baseline per profile, or merged - TBD)\n- Handle wrapper profiles (InSpec profiles that depend on other profiles)\n- May share parsing logic with legacyhdf-to-hdf or may replace it once legacy migration is complete\n\nDesign question: should this share code with legacyhdf-to-hdf or be independent? The legacyhdf converter handles HDF v1 data that was already processed by Heimdall, which may differ slightly from raw InSpec output.", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-41z", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_s