{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "196d8d15a17787c70bb5a3de68f16bf6ce5df751d0bf3be5564bf0d042e35c43", "created_at": "2026-02-08 14:00:52", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "Filter-based partitioning for projects with true >10,000 issues is not yet implemented.\n\nWhat was done: fetcher caps pagination at maxPages=10,000 (ps=500 per page = up to 5M issues). For most real projects this is sufficient.\n\nWhat remains: if a project hits the Elasticsearch 10k result limit on a single unfiltered query, the API will return at most 10,000 issues regardless of page count. To handle those projects, we need to split queries by severity/type/language/date range and merge results. This is the original scope of this issue.\n\nReference: https://community.sonarsource.com/t/how-to-retrieve-more-than-10-000-results-using-api-issues-search/153628\n", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-6b0.21.1", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "open", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Address SonarQube 10,000 record limit", "updated_at": "2026-03-06 21:07:28", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "All fetcher and converter tests use httptest.NewServer with canned JSON responses. contextCapturingSonarqubeTransport RoundTripper added to verify timeout behavior. No live SonarQube server required for any test.", "closed_at": "2026-02-20 15:21:33", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "335e2fa7f1a801a8b2d9d29d54e2b519e6f069dda9b919191a8d59a277be524f", "created_at": "2026-02-08 14:01:03", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "Create static SonarQube API response fixtures (JSON files) instead of requiring a mock server. Mock API endpoints directly using MSW or similar for TypeScript/Go. Capture real SonarQube responses for different scenarios (branch, PR, main project).\n\nCurrent heimdall2 approach requires running 'yarn run cypress-test mock-json' to start a mock HTTP server on port 3001, which is cumbersome for testing.\n\nGoal: Enable converter testing with static fixtures, no server required.", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-6b0.21.2", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "Research completed 2026-02-10. See TESTING-RESEARCH.md in sonarqube-to-hdf directory.\n\nKey findings:\n- Our approach is already superior to Heimdall2 (static fixtures vs mock server)\n- DefectDojo provides gold standard with 17+ test fixtures covering edge cases\n- Need to expand fixtures: empty results, large datasets, hotspots, multiple projects\n- Should follow DefectDojo's pattern: real API captures, comprehensive edge cases\n- No mock server needed - static JSON is better (faster, reliable, version controlled)\n\nNext steps: Create expanded fixture set following recommendations in research doc.", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Improve SonarQube testing without live server", "updated_at": "2026-02-20 15:21:33", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
