{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "Fixed: URL double-encoding (RawPath), cross-platform glab config (adrg/xdg), hostname-with-port matching. Commit 90996ed.", "closed_at": "2026-03-01 22:58:57", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "f00c9b515da160e4da4f6bfd54ab31f4902595dd5b6130178f2780be753eb111", "created_at": "2026-03-01 17:49:31", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "## Bug\nWhen using `--project wdower/juice-shop` (namespace/path format), the GitLab fetcher returns 404. Numeric project IDs (`--project 1`) work fine.\n\n## Root Cause\nIn `hdf-cli/internal/fetchers/gitlab.go`, line ~139-148: `url.PathEscape(f.params.ProjectID)` produces `wdower%2Fjuice-shop`, which is then assigned to `url.URL.Path`. When Go serializes the URL via `.String()`, it re-encodes the `%` to `%25`, producing `wdower%252Fjuice-shop` in the actual HTTP request. GitLab doesn't find that project ID, returns 404.\n\n## Fix\nSet both `url.URL.Path` (decoded) and `url.URL.RawPath` (pre-encoded) so Go preserves the intended encoding. Or construct the URL string directly without going through `url.URL`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `hdf fetch gitlab --project wdower/juice-shop ...` works (namespace/path format)\n- [ ] `hdf fetch gitlab --project 1 ...` still works (numeric ID)\n- [ ] Test added for namespace/path project IDs with slashes\n- [ ] Existing fetcher tests still pass", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-7pk", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "bug", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Fix double URL-encoding of project path in GitLab fetcher", "updated_at": "2