{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "Schema designed and implemented", "closed_at": "2026-03-14 17:19:45", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "ef3b08051607d490810f152b1aa92d59b8915b044db4e62c8ebb22dca4d7818a", "created_at": "2026-03-14 01:33:54", "created_by": "Aaron Lippold", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "Design and formalize the hdf-comparison JSON schema as a new HDF document type.\n\nResearch found no industry standard for structured security assessment comparison:\n- SARIF annotates results inline, no standalone diff document\n- RFC 6902 is structural only, no security semantics\n- No security tool (Snyk, Grype, DefectDojo, etc.) has a public diff schema\n\nThis positions HDF as the first formal schema for security assessment comparison.\n\nKey design elements:\n- Terraform-inspired before/after snapshots (not patches)\n- SARIF-compatible state vocabulary (new, unchanged, updated, absent, fixed, regressed)\n- Configurable matching strategies with confidence scores\n- 4 comparison modes: temporal, baseline, fleet, multiSource\n- Drift vs changes separation (Terraform pattern)\n- Multi-scanner conflict preservation (Automerge pattern)\n- HDF integrity integration (signed diffs for audit trails)\n\nDesign doc: docs/plans/2026-03-13-hdf-diff-schema-design.md", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-e2e", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "feature", "metadata": {}, "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "lippold@gmail.com", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 1, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Design hdf-comparison schema (formal diff document type)", "updated_at": "2026-03-14 17:19:45", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
