{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "Implemented in a2b2d82 \u2014 handles missing ruleId (Gitleaks), empty locations (Dockle), and message.id+messageStrings (SpotBugs)", "closed_at": "2026-02-23 00:11:03", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "64eeda6ab87fec35d2d6742b6492eb70287e19f78dd7e178b70084ea89e180b9", "created_at": "2026-02-22 12:43:31", "created_by": "Will", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "SpotBugs SARIF output uses message.id with arguments instead of message.text. Per the SARIF 2.1.0 spec, when message.text is absent, the converter should resolve the message from rule.messageStrings[message.id] and substitute positional arguments. Currently the TypeScript converter crashes (fixed with null-safety fallback) and Go silently produces empty titles/descriptions. Test fixture: spotbugs.sarif from DefectDojo.", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-of5", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "SARIF converter: support message.id + messageStrings lookup", "updated_at": "2026-02-23 00:11:03", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "SARIF converter enriched with full 2.1.0 spec support. Remaining shared format converters (JUnit, CycloneDX, XCCDF) will be built as standalone tasks before individual tool converters.", "closed_at": "2026-02-21 14:58:33", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "6e36985c9ff93ddc66d1d2adddbd1317407480a8c4c1f520c77951aff5bd3bdd", "created_at": "2026-02-20 20:56:47", "created_by": "Will", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "## Architecture Decision: Format-Level Routing\n\n### Problem\nMany security tools output multiple formats (native JSON, SARIF, SonarQube Generic, etc.). Users shouldn't need to know which converter to use \u2014 `hdf convert gosec to hdf` should work regardless of whether the input is gosec native JSON or gosec SARIF output.\n\n### Decision: Strategy B \u2014 Rich shared format converters + tool-level format detection\n\nTool converters (e.g. gosec-to-hdf) become thin routing layers:\n1. Detect what format the input is in (native JSON? SARIF? JUnit XML?)\n2. If shared format \u2192 delegate to shared format converter\n3. If native \u2192 use tool-specific parsing\n4. Optionally apply tool-specific enrichment after shared conversion\n\n### Shared Format Converters Needed\n- **SARIF** (covers: gosec, snyk, zap, jfrog-xray, semgrep, CodeQL, trivy, checkov, ESLint, fortify, veracode)\n- **JUnit XML** (covers: test frameworks, CI/CD outputs)\n- **CycloneDX** (covers: SBOM tools \u2014 trivy, syft, snyk, cdxgen)\n- **XCCDF** (covers: OpenSCAP, DISA STIGs)\n\n### SARIF Converter Gaps (current \u2192 needed)\nCurrent converter is minimal. Must add:\n- `rules[]` definitions (name, description, helpUri)\n- `rules[].relationships` \u2192 CWE taxonomy extraction\n- `tool.driver.supportedTaxonomies` \u2192 CWE/OWASP awareness\n- `result.suppressions[]` \u2192 notReviewed status with justification\n- `rules[].properties` \u2192 confidence, tags, custom metadata\n- `rules[].defaultConfiguration.level` \u2192 severity when result.level is absent\n- Proper severity granularity from rule metadata\n\n### Impact on Converter Count\n- ~14 proprietary-only tools still need dedicated converters\n- ~5-8 SARIF-capable tools can delegate to enriched SARIF converter\n- 3 standard formats (JUnit, CycloneDX, XCCDF) get dedicated shared converters\n- Net: fewer converters to build and maintain\n\n### Format Detection\nUse fingerprinting (check for `$schema`+`version`+`runs` for SARIF, `<testsuites>` for JUnit, `bomFormat` for CycloneDX, etc.) rather than requiring the user to specify format.\n\n---\n## Progress\n- [x] SARIF converter enriched with full spec support (2026-02-21): rules[], relationships, taxonomies, suppressions, kind mapping, fixes, codeFlows, snippets, fingerprints, level fallback chain\n- [ ] JUnit XML shared format converter\n- [ ] CycloneDX shared format converter\n- [ ] XCCDF shared format converter", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-oi8", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Audit converters for format-level commonality", "updated_at": "2026-02-22 19:22:55", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
