{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "ab04f3ef2429174f816aa7672a5bb1bd4807d1f748e4a86ee38fe563e3bcbe57", "created_at": "2026-02-18 22:30:00", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "Mutation testing is now configured for all packages. This bead tracks integration into the CI pipeline.\n\n## Tools installed\n- **Go**: Gremlins (`~/go/bin/gremlins`, install: `go install github.com/go-gremlins/gremlins/cmd/gremlins@latest`)\n- **TypeScript**: Stryker (`@stryker-mutator/core` + `@stryker-mutator/vitest-runner`)\n- **Configs**: `stryker.config.cjs` exists in hdf-utilities, hdf-mappings, hdf-validators, hdf-parsers\n\n## Recommended CI integration\n\n### Option A: Scheduled nightly run (simplest)\nAdd a GitHub Actions workflow that runs on schedule:\n```yaml\non:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: '0 2 * * *'  # 2am daily\njobs:\n  mutation:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-go@v5\n      - run: go install github.com/go-gremlins/gremlins/cmd/gremlins@latest\n      - run: pnpm install\n      - run: pnpm build\n      # Run gremlins on each Go module\n      - run: cd hdf-cli && gremlins unleash --timeout-coefficient 20 --threshold-efficacy 100\n      # Run stryker on TS packages\n      - run: cd hdf-utilities && npx stryker run\n```\n\n### Option B: Incremental on PRs (more sophisticated)\n- Gremlins: `gremlins unleash --diff main` \u2014 only tests mutations in lines changed vs main\n- Stryker: `npx stryker run --incremental` \u2014 reuses previous results, only re-runs changed mutants\n- Store incremental files as CI artifacts or commit them to the repo\n\n## Notes\n- `pnpm lint` in pre-commit hook already gates commits; mutation testing is too slow for pre-commit\n- Gremlins `--timeout-coefficient 20` is required (default causes all tests to time out in this repo due to fast coverage baseline)\n- hdf-validators must update `assert` \u2192 `with` syntax (hdf-libs-n09) before Stryker can run on it\n- Current baseline scores: Go all 100% efficacy; TS: utilities 77.68%, mappings 72.48%, parsers 50% (unit only)", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-t0t", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 3, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "open", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Integrate mutation testing into CI (scheduled / incremental)", "updated_at": "2026-02-22 19:22:57", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "Format detection utility and gosec SARIF routing complete. Remaining SARIF-capable tools will integrate format detection as part of their individual converter beads.", "closed_at": "2026-02-21 14:58:32", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "587ae51738e8b02333c439a0c62477a930763c5179813e0e77064b7d5ea5f769", "created_at": "2026-02-21 13:20:13", "created_by": "Will", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "Tool converters (e.g. gosec-to-hdf) should detect the input format and delegate to shared format converters when appropriate.\n\n## Design\nEach tool converter's Convert function:\n1. Runs format fingerprinting on input bytes (is it SARIF? JUnit XML? CycloneDX? native?)\n2. If shared format \u2192 delegates to the shared format converter (e.g. sarif-to-hdf)\n3. If native \u2192 uses tool-specific parsing\n4. Optionally applies tool-specific enrichment after shared conversion\n\n## Fingerprinting Heuristics\n- SARIF: JSON with $schema containing \"sarif\" OR top-level version (string) + runs (array)\n- JUnit XML: XML with <testsuites> or <testsuite> root element\n- CycloneDX: JSON with bomFormat field OR XML with CycloneDX namespace\n- XCCDF: XML with XCCDF namespace\n- Native: tool-specific detection (e.g. gosec has GosecVersion + Issues fields)\n\n## Shared format converter location\nhdf-converters/formats/{sarif,junit,cyclonedx,xccdf}/{go,typescript}/\n\n## Affected tool converters (SARIF-capable)\ngosec, snyk, zap, jfrog-xray, fortify, veracode + any future tool that supports SARIF export\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires enriched SARIF converter (comprehensive rules/relationships/suppressions/taxonomy parsing)\n- Existing tool-specific converters continue working for native format input\n\n---\n\n## Progress\n- [x] Format detection utility (Go + TypeScript) in shared/go/formatdetect.go, shared/typescript/formatdetect.ts\n- [x] gosec converter routes SARIF input to shared SARIF converter (Go + TypeScript)\n- [x] Tests: format detection unit tests (13 Go, 11 TS), gosec SARIF routing integration tests\n- [ ] Other SARIF-capable tool converters (snyk, zap, jfrog-xray, etc.) \u2014 pending those converters being built", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-t7h", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "task", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "closed", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Implement format detection and routing in tool converters", "updated_at": "2026-02-22 19:22:58", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
