{"acceptance_criteria": "", "actor": "", "agent_state": "", "await_id": "", "await_type": "", "close_reason": "", "closed_by_session": "", "compaction_level": 0, "content_hash": "90b2a161c1e53401280c207dfee53dbd2240a933c672e626d1a9789f056e7458", "created_at": "2026-02-06 14:39:55", "created_by": "Will Dower", "crystallizes": 0, "description": "Enhance hdf-cli commands to process multiple files in a single invocation with summary reporting.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Input Methods\n- Multiple file arguments: `hdf validate file1.json file2.json file3.json`\n- Glob patterns: `hdf validate scans/*.json` or `hdf validate \"**/*-results.json\"`\n\n### Output Formats\n- **Default**: Summary table showing per-file results\n  ```\n  Validating 10 files...\n  \u2713 scan-1.json         (results)\n  \u2713 scan-2.json         (results)\n  \u2717 scan-3.json         (results) - baselines[0].name: is required\n  \n  Results: 8/10 passed, 2 failed\n  ```\n- **--json**: JSON output for scripting/automation\n- **--yaml**: YAML output as alternative structured format\n\n### Error Handling\n- Continue processing all files even if some fail\n- Exit with non-zero code if ANY files fail\n- Research and use correct GNU-style exit codes:\n  - 0 = all files processed successfully\n  - Non-zero = at least one file failed\n  - Different codes for different failure types?\n\n### Processing\n- Sequential processing (not parallel)\n- Progress indication for large batches\n\n### Commands to Update\n- `hdf validate` - validate multiple HDF files\n- `hdf stats` - aggregate statistics across multiple files\n- `hdf info` - show info for multiple files\n- `hdf query` - query across multiple files\n- `hdf list` - list requirements across multiple files\n- ~~`hdf convert`~~ - skip (requires output file argument, complex)\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### File Expansion\n- Need to handle glob patterns correctly\n- Handle file not found errors gracefully\n- Validate that globs match at least one file\n\n### Exit Codes Research\nResearch proper GNU/POSIX exit codes:\n- Standard: 0 = success, 1 = general error\n- Consider: Different codes for validation vs I/O errors?\n- Look at tools like: grep, find, ls for precedent\n\n### Output Format Consistency\n- All bulk operations should use similar output structure\n- --json format should be consistent across commands\n- --yaml should mirror JSON structure\n\n### Testing\n- Test with large numbers of files (100+)\n- Test with glob patterns that match nothing\n- Test with mix of valid and invalid files\n- Test with --json and --yaml output parsing\n\n## Examples\n\n```bash\n# Validate multiple files\nhdf validate scan1.json scan2.json scan3.json\n\n# Validate with glob\nhdf validate scans/*.json\n\n# JSON output for CI/CD\nhdf validate \"**/*.json\" --json > results.json\n\n# Stats across multiple files\nhdf stats scan-*.json\n\n# Query across files\nhdf query \"baselines[0].name\" results/*.json\n```\n\n## Success Criteria\n- Multiple file arguments work for all commands\n- Glob patterns expand correctly\n- Summary table is clear and useful\n- --json output is valid and parseable\n- Exit codes follow GNU conventions\n- All existing single-file functionality preserved\n- Tests cover bulk operations", "design": "", "ephemeral": 0, "event_kind": "", "hook_bead": "", "id": "hdf-libs-xm3", "is_template": 0, "issue_type": "feature", "metadata": "{}", "mol_type": "", "notes": "", "owner": "will@dower.dev", "payload": "", "pinned": 0, "priority": 2, "rig": "", "role_bead": "", "role_type": "", "sender": "", "source_repo": "", "source_system": "", "spec_id": "", "status": "open", "target": "", "timeout_ns": 0, "title": "Add bulk file operations to hdf-cli", "updated_at": "2026-02-22 19:22:59", "waiters": "", "wisp_type": "", "work_type": ""}
